<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$131.6m.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$131.6m.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian promissory note issuance surged on Wednesday to A$131.6 million, its highest total this month.</p>
<p>Boral Ltd lead the charge, selling A$40 million worth of its December 19-dated paper at five to six basis points over the mid-rate for the closest corresponding bank bill.</p>
<p>The physical bank bill yield curve has moved lower after the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee decided on Tuesday to hold interest rates steady, but discount securities dealers said turnover remained moderate.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors are standing aside from the market. They are investing short or staying in cash,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
